From: Gabriel Lafond-Thenaille <gabriel@videolabs.io>
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: increase GGML_MAX_NAME from 64 to 96

Some T5-based GGUF models (e.g. google/madlad400-3b-mt) contain tensor
names that exceed the 64-character limit enforced by gguf_init_from_file_impl,
causing the model to fail loading with:

  gguf_init_from_file_impl: tensor name N is too long: 68 >= 64

The offending tensors are the relative attention bias weights whose
HuggingFace names are 68 characters long:

  encoder.block.0.layer.0.SelfAttention.relative_attention_bias.weight
  decoder.block.0.layer.0.SelfAttention.relative_attention_bias.weight

Raising GGML_MAX_NAME to 96 accommodates these names. The macro is
guarded by #ifndef so downstream users can still override it.
---
 include/ggml.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/ggml.h
+++ b/include/ggml.h
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
 #define GGML_MAX_OP_PARAMS      64
 
 #ifndef GGML_MAX_NAME
-#   define GGML_MAX_NAME        64
+#   define GGML_MAX_NAME        96
 #endif
 
 #define GGML_DEFAULT_N_THREADS  4
